<title>GERMANY: Merrill denies downgrading Volkswagen.</title>
<headline>Merrill denies downgrading Volkswagen.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch on Thursday denied market speculation that it had downgraded German carmaker Volkswagen AG.</p>
<p>European auto sector analyst Stephen Reitman said he remained very positive on Volkswagen.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe there is a lot of potential left in the stock,&quot; he said in response to a Reuters query.</p>
<p>Rumours of a downgrade by a London investment bank put pressure on VW shares on Thursday.</p>
<p>At 1323 GMT, VW was down 19.50 marks at 1,446 marks while the IBIS DAX share index was up 0.24 percent at 4,233.89 points.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
